## Scenario 1 — Installation and Setup

### What Was Built
Installed and configured a full XAMPP web stack and osTicket helpdesk system on DC01, accessible from Client01 across the internal network.

### Steps Performed

#### Part A — File Transfer via VirtualBox Shared Folder
1. Downloaded XAMPP and osTicket on Windows 11 host machine
2. Created `C:\LabFiles` folder on host
3. Configured VirtualBox Shared Folder — mapped as Z: drive on DC01
4. Installed VirtualBox Guest Additions on DC01 to enable shared folder access
5. Confirmed both files visible on DC01 via Z: drive

#### Part B — XAMPP Installation
6. Ran XAMPP installer from shared folder
7. Installed with Apache, MySQL, PHP and phpMyAdmin components
8. Started Apache and MySQL services from XAMPP Control Panel
9. Verified both services running green

#### Part C — Database Setup
10. Opened phpMyAdmin at `http://localhost/phpmyadmin`
11. Created new database named `osticket`
12. Set MySQL root password via command line for osTicket installer

#### Part D — osTicket Installation
13. Copied osTicket upload folder to `C:\xampp\htdocs\osticket`
14. Renamed `ost-sampleconfig.php` to `ost-config.php`
15. Ran osTicket installer at `http://localhost/osticket/setup`
16. Completed prerequisites check — PHP 8.0.30 and MySQLi confirmed
17. Filled in Basic Installation form:
    - Helpdesk Name: Mayank Lab Helpdesk
    - Admin: Mayank Rale (mayank.admin)
18. Connected to osticket database with root credentials
19. Installation completed successfully

#### Part E — Post-Installation Configuration
20. Deleted setup directory for security
21. Added Windows Firewall rule to allow port 80 from Client01
22. Logged into Admin Control Panel
23. Created helpdesk agent — John Smith (jsmith)
24. Assigned John Smith to Support department

### Troubleshooting Notes
- PHP execution timeout (120s) increased to 300s in php.ini to allow installation to complete
- Windows Firewall rule added to allow ICMP and HTTP traffic from Client01
- VirtualBox Guest Additions required for shared folder functionality

