## Scenario 2 — Helpdesk Ticketing

### What Was Simulated
Simulated a complete helpdesk ticket lifecycle — a user raises a ticket reporting a network drive issue, the helpdesk agent receives and assigns it, posts a resolution, and closes the ticket.

### Steps Performed

#### Part A — Raise a Ticket (Client01)
1. Opened osTicket Support Center on Client01 at `http://192.168.1.10/osticket`
2. Clicked **Open a New Ticket**
3. Filled in ticket details:
   - User: John Smith (jsmith@mayanklab.local)
   - Help Topic: General Enquiry
   - Issue: Cannot access shared network drive
   - Details: Getting access denied error when trying to connect

#### Part B — Assign the Ticket (DC01)
4. Logged into Agent Panel on DC01 at `http://localhost/osticket/scp`
5. Viewed ticket in Open queue
6. Opened ticket and reviewed details
7. Assigned ticket to John Smith agent

#### Part C — Resolve the Ticket (DC01)
8. Posted resolution reply:
   - Investigated the issue with shared network drive access
   - Problem caused by incorrect drive mapping settings
   - Remapped the drive and verified access restored
9. Changed ticket status from **Open** to **Resolved**
10. Posted reply — ticket marked resolved

#### Part D — Close the Ticket
11. Ticket moved to Closed queue automatically
12. Verified ticket appearing in Closed tickets list
13. Confirmed full ticket history visible including timestamps and resolution notes

